[2026-01-15T13:50:35.932979] PLAN PHASE analysis:

Smith-Waterman has classic DP dependencies:
- constructMatrix: H[i][j] depends on H[i-1][j-1], H[i-1][j], H[i][j-1]
  → Anti-diagonal (wavefront) parallelism is natural
  → All cells on same anti-diagonal i+j=k are independent
  → Can parallelize each wavefront sweep
- findHighestScore: embarrassingly parallel reduction (max + position)
- traceback: inherently sequential (single path walk backward)

CHOSEN STRATEGY: Anti-diagonal wavefront parallelism in constructMatrix + parallel reduction in findHighestScore
- Fits within 1 file patch (~150 LOC change)
- Deterministic: fixed anti-diagonal order, fixed reduction order for max
- Safe: respects true dependencies
- Perf: O(n*m) work on ~min(n,m) wavefronts → good parallelism for square-ish matrices

REJECTED ALTERNATIVES:
1. Row-level parallelism (simple #pragma omp parallel for on outer loop): violates row dependencies (H[i][j] needs H[i-1][*])
2. Task-based DAG (OpenMP tasks): higher overhead, same dependency structure as wavefront, exceeds simplicity goal
3. Tile/block parallelism: complex data layout changes, >250 LOC

Small-N threshold: if n*m < 10000, sequential (overhead dominates)
Worker bound: default OpenMP threads (≤ core count)

